Edit or create a file in the in-world filesystem.

usage: @fedit <path>

Opens the online string editor on the file at an absolute path in the
in-world filesystem (the VFS). The editor is seeded with the file's current
contents; a path that does not exist yet starts empty and is created when
you save. This is how you author a Kobold source for @compile without host
access.

In the editor, type to add lines; /s saves, /a aborts, /h shows the help.
On save the file is written and committed to the VFS. On abort the file is
left unchanged.

  <path>    an absolute VFS path, for example /src/foo.kp

Wizard only. It writes the shared in-world tree that programs launch and
compile from. A file larger than the editor's buffer (16 KB) cannot be
edited here. This is the line editor boris ships; a full-screen editor may
be offered later for capable terminal clients.

Example:
  @fedit /src/greet.kp
      Edit (or create) the Kobold source, then @compile /src/greet.kp greet.

See also @compile, @setverb, help kobold.
